{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ABxSVJRHCWsnGXgpfZ59BK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read the full paper and the review context YAML. Let me summarize what I have:\n\n**Paper**: \"ProgressProbe: Weakly-Supervised Temporal Progress Estimation for LLM Agent Trajectories\"\n\n**Key contributions**:\n1. A data-programming framework transferring Snorkel to sequential agent trajectories with 3 LFs\n2. A lightweight GRU probe with attention that learns temporal progress signals from noisy labels\n3. Cross-agent transfer (SWE-agent → OpenHands)\n\n**Experiments in paper**:\n- Table 1: Results on 400-window human gold set\n\n\n- Tables 2-14: Comprehensive ablations and analyses covering label quality, baseline comparisons, temporal aggregation, cross-agent transfer, early termination tradeoffs, error analysis, labeling function dynamics, and architectural choices\n- Tables 15-16: SupCon ablation, feature type comparisons, and data scaling experiments\n- Mapping experiments from the config to their corresponding tables, with most ablations already covered and window size analysis still pending\n- The paper appears to comprehensively address all the planned experiments, including error analysis, cross-agent transfer, architecture variations, and interpretability visualizations\n\n.\n\nNow I'm setting up the review process by assigning one reviewer to evaluate the methods and experimental design, while another focuses on assessing the novelty and positioning relative to existing work. I'll run both reviews in parallel to move forward efficiently.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14358,"cache_read_input_tokens":41371,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14358},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostic