{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ABxSVJRHCWsnGXgpfZ59BK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"论文和实验设计参考已读完。论文覆盖了 review_context.yaml 中几乎所有想象实验（16/16）。现在启动双 Reviewer 并行审稿。"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14358,"cache_read_input_tokens":41371,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14358},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37dd1f71-0479-4eaf-8dec-0b477d2b7a27","uuid":"100b165c-13c4-43d5-a2d8-4c6bb2e9ffd9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ABxSVJRHCWsnGXgpfZ59BK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013y6GiByD2h9oKVGAZ9ffpa","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for a top ML venue peer review. Your focus is **Methods and Experiments**. Evaluate the paper \"ProgressProbe: Weakly-Supervised Temporal Progress Estimation for LLM Agent Trajectories\" using the 6-point scale (1=Strong Reject, 6=Strong Accept; acceptance threshold ~25%).\n\n## Paper Summary\nThe paper proposes ProgressProbe, a framework for detecting \"semantic stagnation\" in LLM agent trajectories (agents executing diverse but collectively ineffective actions). Two contributions:\n1. A data-programming pipeline transferring Snorkel to sequential agent trajectories, using 3 labeling functions (file_diff_delta, command_repetition, outcome_backpropagation) to produce window-level progress/stagnation labels via majority vote.\n2. A lightweight GRU probe with attention (1.32M params, ~12 min training) that learns temporal progress signals from these noisy labels.\n\n## Key Results (from paper)\n- **Human gold set (400 windows, 3 annotators, Fleiss κ=0.724)**: Probe 0.862 macro-F1, beating Repeat-3 by +6.89pp, LF Oracle by +4.36pp, Claude Sonnet 4 few-shot by +2.11pp (Table 1)\n- **MV label quality**: 84.5% accuracy vs gold, κ=0.724 (Table 2)\n- **MV labels**: conf≥2 probe 0.906 F1, full data 0.874 F1, both >6pp over Repeat-3 (Table 3)\n- **LLM-as-Judge**: Probe beats Claude S4 few-shot by +3.74pp at 31x lower cost, 606x lower latency (Table 4)\n- **Temporal vs static**: GRU 0.906 vs Mean-pool+LR 0.768, gap=13.72pp; stagnation F1 0.859 vs 0.657 (Table 5)\n- **Cross-agent transfer**: SWE-agent→OpenHands zero-shot 0.835 F1, -7.08pp from within-agent but still +4.53pp over Repeat-3 (Table 6)\n- **Early termination**: Optimal threshold 0.6 saves 32.7% tokens, preserves 96.1% success; intervention paradox: 17.3% terminated trajectories would have resolved but at 2,847 extra tokens (Table 7)\n- **Error analysis**: 221 errors (7.2%), FP=98 (exploratory behavior), FN=123 (diverse ineffective cmds); probe uniquely corrects 187 cases vs Repeat-3 (Tables 8-9)\n- **LF temporal dynamics**: cmd_rep leads by 1.8 steps, file_diff coincident, outcome_bp lags 2.1 steps; onset agreement 34%→peak 71% (Table 10)\n- **Ablations**: Window k=5 sweet spot (Table 11); GRU+Att vs Transformer differ by 0.88pp (Table 12); LF hold-one-out shows all contribute, file_diff most at -4.21pp (Table 13); SupCon +1.31pp (Table 14); Non-NLP features only 0.723 F1 (Table 15); Data scaling saturates ~60% (Table 16)\n\n## Experiment Design Reference\nThe review_context.yaml lists 16 imagined experiments. The paper covers all 16. Key experiments:\n- Full-data generalization (conf≥1 vs conf≥2)\n- LF Oracle baseline\n- LLM-as-Judge (Claude S4 + GPT-4o, zero/few-shot)\n- Mean-pool+LR/SVM baselines\n- Error analysis by pattern type\n- Cross-agent transfer (SWE-agent→OpenHands, 48,352 windows)\n- Window size ablation (k=3,5,7)\n- Architecture ablation (GRU+Att, Transformer, GRU+Mean-pool, MLP)\n- LF hold-one-out\n- SupCon ablation\n- Non-NLP baseline (18 structural features)\n- Data scaling (10/25/50/100%)\n- Early termination simulation\n- Interpretability (t-SNE, attention weights)\n- Human-annotated gold set (400 windows, 3 annotators)\n- LF temporal dynamics\n\n## Your Task\nWrite a structured review covering:\n\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Strengths** (methods + experiments focus, numbered)\n3. **Weaknesses** (methods + experiments focus, numbered)\n4. **Questions to Authors** (numbered)\n5. **Minor Issues**\n6. **Scores**: Soundness (1-5), Presentation (1-5), Contribution (1-5), Overall (1-6), Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous. Focus on:\n- Is the experimental methodology sound? Any circularity concerns?\n- Are baselines comprehensive and fairly compared?\n- Is the GRU probe architecture well-motivated vs alternatives?\n- Are the claims well-supported by evidence?\n- Statistical rigor (variance, significance tests, multiple runs)?\n- Data leakage or confounding concerns?\n- Reproducibility\n\nNote: The frozen sentence encoder used for embeddings is not named in the paper — flag this.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14358,"cache_read_input_tokens":41371,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14358},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37dd1f71-0479-4eaf-8dec-0b477d2b7a27","uuid":"a4716479-a8c8-4a95-9835-ccf521aab7a0"}
