solved but at 2,847 extra tokens (Table 7)\n- **Error analysis**: 221 errors (7.2%), FP=98 (exploratory behavior), FN=123 (diverse ineffective cmds); probe uniquely corrects 187 cases vs Repeat-3 (Tables 8-9)\n- **LF temporal dynamics**: cmd_rep leads by 1.8 steps, file_diff coincident, outcome_bp lags 2.1 steps; onset agreement 34%→peak 71% (Table 10)\n- **Ablations**: Window k=5 sweet spot (Table 11); GRU+Att vs Transformer differ by 0.88pp (Table 12); LF hold-one-out shows all contribute, file_diff most at -4.21pp (Table 13); SupCon +1.31pp (Table 14); Non-NLP features only 0.723 F1 (Table 15); Data scaling saturates ~60% (Table 16)\n\n## Experiment Design Reference\nThe review_context.yaml lists 16 imagined experiments. The paper covers all 16. Key experiments:\n- Full-data generalization (conf≥1 vs conf≥2)\n- LF Oracle baseline\n- LLM-as-Judge (Claude S4 + GPT-4o, zero/few-shot)\n- Mean-pool+LR/SVM baselines\n- Error analysis by pattern type\n- Cross-agent transfer (SWE-agent→OpenHands, 48,352 windows)\n- Window size ablation (k=3,5,7)\n- Architecture ablation (GRU+Att, Transformer, GRU+Mean-pool, MLP)\n- LF hold-one-out\n- SupCon ablation\n- Non-NLP baseline (18 structural features)\n- Data scaling (10/25/50/100%)\n- Early termination simulation\n- Interpretability (t-SNE, attention weights)\n- Human-annotated gold set (400 windows, 3 annotators)\n- LF temporal dynamics\n\n## Your Task\nWrite a structured review covering:\n\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Strengths** (methods + experiments focus, numbered)\n3. **Weaknesses** (methods + experiments focus, numbered)\n4. **Questions to Authors** (numbered)\n5. **Minor Issues**\n6. **Scores**: Soundness (1-5), Presentation (1-5), Contribution (1-5), Overall (1-6), Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous. Focus on:\n- Is the experimental methodology sound? Any circularity concerns?\n- Are baselines comprehensive and fairly compared?\n- Is the GRU probe architecture well-motivated vs alternatives?\n- Are the claims well-supported by evidence?\n- Statistical rigor (variance, significance tests, multiple runs)?\n- Data leakage or confounding concerns?\n- Reproducibility\n\nNote: The frozen sentence encoder used for embeddings is not named in the paper — flag this.\n","uuid":"8f675979-63c3-49d4-90de-0bb8c3dbc232","session_id":"37dd1f71-0479-4eaf-8dec-0b477d2b7a27"}
