{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GzuZEjUFEqAK9eUwydEsa9","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/ROADMAP.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# agent_progress_probe — Research Dashboard\\\\n\\\\n> 最后更新: 2026-05-14 08:17 UTC | 更新原因: MVP 通过，进入 research 阶段，post-MVP kickoff（framing + plan + dream）\\\\n\\\\n## 核心方向\\\\nProgressProbe: 弱监督标注框架 + 轻量 GRU probe，在 sliding window 级别检测 LLM agent 的 progress stagnation。双贡献：(1) Data programming 范式迁移到 agent trajectory；(2) 系统性实证研究（跨实现迁移 + 可解释性分析）。详见 paper_framing.md。\\\\n\\\\n## 当前阶段\\\\n🔬 **Research** — MVP 通过（D007），post-MVP kickoff 进行中\\\\n\\\\n## 当前进展\\\\n- MVP 通过：GRU probe macro-F1=0.9055，比 Repeat-3 高 6.24pp（D007）\\\\n- paper_framing.md 已写（3 Core Claims: 弱监督框架 / window-level 时序建模 / 跨实现迁移）\\\\n- experiment_plan.yaml 已写（P0×8 / P1×5 / P2×4 实验）\\\\n- Dream 模拟已启动（dream_20260514T081656, review_mode=full），等待审稿报告\\\\n- GPU: gpu-5090-2x-2（RTX 5090 32G × 2）已配置\\\\n\\\\n## 近期任务\\\\n- [ ] 等 Dream 完成 → 按审稿报告调整 framing/plan\\\\n- [ ] Dream 通过后批准 P0 实验启动\\\\n- [ ] P0 实验列表：probe-002（全量数据）/ baseline-lf-oracle / baseline-llm-judge / baseline-meanpool-lr / error-analysis / cross-agent\\\\n- [ ] 向用户确认时间线（EMNLP ARR 5/25 vs ACL ARR 8月）\\\\n\\\\n## MVP 结果摘要\\\\n| Method | Macro-F1 | Note |\\\\n|--------|----------|------|\\\\n| GRU Probe | 0.9055 | conf≥2, 15,401 windows |\\\\n| Repeat-3 | 0.8432 | 最强 baseline |\\\\n| Random | 0.4955 | |\\\\n| Majority | 0.4233 | |\\\\n| CosineSim | 0.3129 | |\\\\n\\\\n## GPU 预算\\\\n- gpu-5090-2x-2: RTX 5090 32G × 2\\\\n- P0 实验预计：~10 GPU-hours + API cost ~$200（LLM-as-judge）\\\\n- P1 消融预计：~7.5 GPU-hours\\\\n- P2 加分项：~2 GPU-hours\\\\n\\\\n## 投稿目标\\\\nEMNLP 2026 ARR long paper — 待用户确认 5/25 vs 8月 cycle\\\\n\\\\n## 关键决策日志\\\\n\\\\n| ID | 日期 | 摘要 | 关联实验 |\\\\n|----|------|------|----------|\\\\n| D007 | 2026-05-14 | MVP 通过：GRU probe macro-F1=0.9055，比最佳 baseline Repe | probe_001 |\\\\n| D006 | 2026-05-14 | Phase 0.5 判定通过（保守指标 81.5% ≥ 80%），启动 Phase 1 | — |\\\\n| D005 | 2026-05-14 | LF 间一致率 40.3% 不阻塞 Phase 0.5 重跑；并行启动 LF 冲突分析，Phase  | — |\\\\n| D004 | 2026-05-14 | Phase 0.5 判定未通过：原始一致率 53% 远低于 80% 门禁，质量报告方法学错误（排除  | — |\\\\n| D003 | 2026-05-14 | 暂停 Phase 0.5/1，修复 LF1 逻辑 bug + 扩展到 5K 随机采样后重跑标签统计 | — |\\\\n| D002 | 2026-05-14 | LF2 替换：test_pass_rate_transition → command_repetit | — |\\\\n| D001 | 2026-05-14 | MVP 验证方案确定：GRU probe on SWE-bench trajectories, F1 | — |\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 1999, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013y6GiByD2h9oKVGAZ9ffpa","session_id":"37dd1f71-0479-4eaf-8dec-0b477d2b7a27","uuid":"71022305-7822-4d89-ac27-545d1ef7afc8","timestamp":"2026-05-14T08:51:40.447Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ABxSVJRHCWsnGXgpfZ59BK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H4Gv7Kqk7M3pqgm4QnxcpS","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 2 (R2) for a top ML venue peer review. Your focus is **Novelty and Related Work**. Evaluate the paper \"ProgressProbe: Weakly-Supervised Temporal Progress Estimation for LLM Agent Trajectories\" using the 6-point scale (1=Strong Reject, 6=Strong Accept; acceptance threshold ~25%).\n\n## Paper Summary\nThe paper proposes ProgressProbe, detecting \"semantic stagnation\" in LLM agent trajectories — agents executing diverse but collectively ineffective actions. Two contributions:\n1. A data-programming pipeline transferring Snorkel's paradigm to sequential agent trajectories, using 3 domain-specific labeling functions (file_diff_delta, command_repetition, outcome_backpropagation). Their majority vote achieves 84.5% accuracy vs human gold labels (Fleiss κ=0.724).\n2. A lightweight GRU probe with attention (1.32M params) trained on these noisy labels, achieving 0.91 macro-F1 on MV labels and 0.86 on human gold set. It beats LF oracle by +4.43pp and Claude Sonnet 4 few-shot by +3.74pp at 31x lower cost. Cross-agent transfer SWE-agent→OpenHands retains 0.835 F1.\n\n## Related Work (from paper, Section 2)\nThree short paragraphs:\n1. **Agent monitoring and intervention**: Chen et al.(2024a) cycle detection, Guo et al.(2024) trajectory anomaly, Luo et al.(2024)/Chen et al.(2024b) reward models. Paper claims these miss semantic stagnation or lose window-level temporal dynamics.\n2. **Data programming and weak supervision**: Snorkel (Ratner et al. 2017, 2019). Claims to be first to apply data programming to sequential trajectory data where LF temporal ordering matters.\n3. **Probing learned representations**: Belinkov (2022). Claims novelty in using probes for deployment rather than analysis.\n\nReferences total: 8 (Yang 2024, Wang 2024, Chen 2024a, Guo 2024, Luo 2024, Chen 2024b, Zhang 2024, Ratner 2017, Ratner 2019, Belinkov 2022) — actually 10 references.\n\n## Key Claims\n1. Weak-supervision framework successfully transfers Snorkel to sequential trajectory domain (non-trivial: LFs exhibit temporal dynamics absent in i.i.d. settings)\n2. Temporal modeling matters: GRU probe learns richer signals than the LFs that trained it (+4.43pp over LF oracle, +13.72pp over mean-pool+LR)\n3. Cross-agent generalization: learned progress signal transfers across agent implementations (SWE-agent→OpenHands)\n\n## Your Task\nWrite a structured review covering:\n\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Strengths** (novelty + related work focus, numbered)\n3. **Weaknesses** (novelty + related work focus, numbered)\n4. **Questions to Authors** (numbered)\n5. **Minor Issues**\n6. **Scores**: Soundness (1-5), Presentation (1-5), Contribution (1-5), Overall (1-6), Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous. Focus on:\n- Is the novelty sufficient for a top venue? Is \"applying Snorkel to trajectories + training a GRU\" novel enough?\n- Is the related work coverage adequate? Missing comparisons?\n- Are there closely related works not cited? (Consider: process reward models like Math-Shepherd, ORM/PRM literature, RL-based value functions for agents, agent scaffolding works like Reflexion/LATS, execution feedback mechanisms)\n- Is the \"semantic stagnation\" framing genuinely new or a rebranding of existing concepts?\n- How does this compare to step-level reward models (ORM/PRM) which also estimate progress?\n- The paper has only 10 references — is this sufficient?\n- Venue fit: the paper targets NLP/ML but the problem is arguably more SE. How well is the NLP angle justified?\n- Is the contribution primarily methodological (framework) or empirical (showing it works)?\n\nBe specific about what related work is missing and how it would change the paper's positioning.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14358,"cache_read_input_tokens":41371,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14358},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37dd1f71-0479-4eaf-8dec-0b477d2b7a27","uuid":"96e9ddea-9274-4515-b189-9e66530fef98"}
